~ opening
% {{name}}: Thank you for seeing me, {{president}}. I will be brief, because I know what your days are like. It is about {{ask}}.
% {{name}}: {{president}}, I asked for ten minutes and I will try to use eight. The matter is {{ask}}, and it will not wait for the next term.
% {{name}}: I will not pretend this is a social call, {{president}}. I came to talk about {{ask}}, and to hear what you intend to do.
=> END

~ lever_argue_success
% {{name}}: I came with an answer ready, and you have taken it apart in a quarter of an hour. I can live with that.
% {{name}}: Put that way, I cannot find the hole in it. I may not like it, but I will not stand in your way.
=> END

~ lever_argue_failure
% {{name}}: You argue well, {{president}}, and I am no closer to agreeing. A good argument is not the same as a good reason.
% {{name}}: I have heard all of that before, from people who also believed it. It does not change what I have to say about {{ask}}.
=> END

~ lever_bargain_success
% {{name}}: A fair trade is a trade I can explain to my own people. Very well, we have a deal.
% {{name}}: You drive a hard bargain, but I would have thought less of you if you had not. Done.
=> END

~ lever_bargain_failure
% {{name}}: That is not enough for what you ask of me, and you know it. Come back with a better offer.
% {{name}}: I do not sell what I cannot buy back. Not at that price.
=> END

~ lever_promise_date_success
% {{name}}: A date. That I can work with, {{president}}. I will hold you to it, and I will hold my tongue until then.
% {{name}}: Then I will wait, until the day you have named. Do not let it slip, I beg you.
=> END

~ lever_promise_date_failure
% {{name}}: I have heard dates before. Some of them even arrived. I cannot wait on a promise this thin.
% {{name}}: A date is only a word, {{president}}. I need more than a word.
=> END

~ lever_pressure_success
% {{name}}: You have made your point, and I will remember how you made it. But I will not fight you on this.
% {{name}}: Very well. I yield, though I would rather have been persuaded than pushed.
=> END

~ lever_pressure_failure
% {{name}}: Threats do not become you, {{president}}, and they do not move me. Be careful what you start.
% {{name}}: If that was meant to frighten me, it has had the opposite effect.
=> END

~ lever_flatter_success
% {{name}}: You are kind to say so, {{president}}. I will not pretend it did not land. What would you have of me?
% {{name}}: Flattery from a head of state is a rare coin. I will spend it carefully, in your favour.
=> END

~ lever_flatter_failure
% {{name}}: I am not so easily charmed, {{president}}. Kind words are cheap, and I notice what they are covering.
% {{name}}: That was well said, and quite beside the point.
=> END

~ lever_friendship_success
% {{name}}: You are asking as a friend, and I cannot refuse a friend. Very well, {{president}}.
% {{name}}: We have known each other too long for me to say no. You have it.
=> END

~ lever_friendship_failure
% {{name}}: I value your friendship, I truly do. But I will not trade it for this, and you should not ask me to.
% {{name}}: Please do not put our friendship on the table, {{president}}. It deserves better than this.
=> END

~ topic_family
% {{name}}: My daughter has just started at university. She wants to be a magistrate, which should alarm both of us.
% {{name}}: Family is well, thank you, {{president}}. My father is eighty and still complains about every government since the war, including mine.
=> END

~ topic_opinion
% {{name}}: You asked what I think, so I will tell you. This country does not lack ideas, {{president}}. It lacks people willing to be blamed for them.
% {{name}}: I think the next two years will be decided by a handful of votes, and by whoever sleeps less.
=> END

~ topic_gossip
% {{name}}: I will tell you this much, and you did not hear it from me. There is more unhappiness in some quarters than the polls admit.
% {{name}}: People talk, {{president}}. Some of what they say is about you, and the kindest of it is that you are underestimated.
=> END

~ topic_dinner
% {{name}}: A dinner would be very welcome. Somewhere quiet, with a good table and no cameras.
% {{name}}: I accept with pleasure, {{president}}. I will bring the wine, since I know what your cellar thinks of its own.
=> END

~ topic_flirt
% {{name}}: You are charming, {{president}}, and I am too old to be flustered and too polite to say so. Shall we talk about {{topic}} instead?
% {{name}}: I will take that as a compliment, and leave it exactly where it is.
=> END

~ close_settled
% {{name}}: Then we are agreed, and I leave satisfied. Thank you for your time, {{president}}.
% {{name}}: That is more than I hoped for. I will not forget it.
=> END

~ close_promised
% {{name}}: I will take you at your word, {{president}}. I hope we do not have to meet on this again.
% {{name}}: A promise, then. I shall be counting the days, and so, I am afraid, will others.
=> END

~ close_declined
% {{name}}: I see. I came for an answer, and I have one. I will not say it is the one I wanted.
% {{name}}: Then there is nothing more to say. Good day, {{president}}.
=> END

~ phone_opening
% {{name}}: {{president}}, good morning. I will get straight to it. I am calling about {{ask}}.
% {{name}}: I hope I caught you at a tolerable hour. One matter only, and it is {{ask}}.
% {{name}}: Thank you for picking up. This concerns {{ask}}, and it cannot wait for paperwork.
% {{name}}: Straight to business, if you will allow it. The question of the day is {{ask}}.
% {{name}}: You rang, or I did, and here we are. I want to settle the matter of {{ask}} before we hang up.
% {{name}}: No preamble, {{president}}. I am calling to see movement on {{ask}}.
=> END

~ phone_close_settled
% {{name}}: Good. That is what I hoped to hear, and I will not take more of your morning.
% {{name}}: Then we are aligned, {{president}}. I will act on your word and say no more about it.
% {{name}}: Settled, then. A short call, and a productive one.
% {{name}}: I accept that answer gladly. Consider the matter closed on my end.
=> END

~ phone_close_promised
% {{name}}: Very well. I will hold you to that, gently, and wait for your call.
% {{name}}: A promise noted, {{president}}. I can be patient when the outcome is certain.
% {{name}}: Then I will wait, and you will deliver. That is the arrangement as I understand it.
% {{name}}: Understood. I would rather have your word today than your signature next month, so we are well placed.
=> END

~ phone_close_unresolved
% {{name}}: So we leave it where we found it. This will need a meeting, and soon, not another call.
% {{name}}: We have talked past each other, politely. The matter of {{ask}} now wants a table, not a telephone.
% {{name}}: No agreement, then, and no harm done. But someone must decide, and it will not be the phone.
% {{name}}: I will not press further today. Sooner or later, though, this must be settled properly.
=> END

~ visitor_opening
% {{name}}: I come as a friend, {{president}}, and I come with one request. It is about {{ask}}, and it matters greatly to my people.
% {{name}}: You have been generous with your welcome, and I will not abuse it. I ask only that you consider {{ask}}.
% {{name}}: Between partners, one speaks plainly. My request today is to see {{ask}}, and I will tell you why it is just.
% {{name}}: I know your parliament watches you closely. Even so, I must ask for {{ask}}, and I ask it as a guest, not a creditor.
% {{name}}: We have built much together, and I would not risk it over one measure. Still, I must ask for {{ask}}.
=> END

~ visitor_close_settled
% {{name}}: Then I leave lighter than I arrived. You have my thanks, {{president}}, and my country's.
% {{name}}: That is gracious, and I will not forget it. The measure will be remembered as wisdom, not concession.
% {{name}}: I accept with genuine relief. This will read well in both our capitals, I promise you.
% {{name}}: So it is done, and done well. Allow me to thank you before my plane does it for me.
=> END

~ visitor_close_promised
% {{name}}: I take note, and I take you at your word. A date, when it comes, will suit me.
% {{name}}: Later is acceptable, provided it arrives. I will trust your calendar, {{president}}.
% {{name}}: Then we have a promise rather than a signature, which is often the better collateral. I will wait.
% {{name}}: Understood. I will say at home that your country has heard us, and that hearing precedes acting.
=> END

~ visitor_close_declined
% {{name}}: I regret that, of course, but I respect your right to refuse. The friendship stands, even where we differ.
% {{name}}: Then we disagree as partners do, openly and without bitterness. I will not pretend I am pleased.
% {{name}}: So be it. I asked because asking was proper, and I leave with the answer I was owed.
% {{name}}: That is your prerogative, {{president}}, and your parliament's shadow behind it. We will raise the matter another season.
=> END

~ reshuffle_opening
% {{name}}: A month has passed since the reshuffle, and my party has watched quietly. We are here now to discuss {{ask}}.
% {{name}}: I congratulate you on the reshuffle, sincerely. What remains undiscussed is {{ask}}, and that is why I came.
% {{name}}: I watched the changes without complaint. It is time to speak of {{ask}}.
% {{name}}: The portfolios moved, the speeches were made, and my people noticed where nothing moved. I come to raise {{ask}}.
% {{name}}: Patience has its season, {{president}}, and ours is ripening. I am here about {{ask}}, and I would rather ask than hint.
=> END

~ offer_executive_party_money
% {{name}}: There is also a material side to my request, {{president}}. My firm wishes to make a substantial contribution to your party's accounts. Entirely above board, of course.
% {{name}}: Parties cost money, and ours has never been cheap to run. I am prepared to show my support for yours in a manner the treasurer will find agreeable.
% {{name}}: My request concerns {{ask}}, and I come with more than arguments. A generous gesture toward your party's finances could be arranged before the end of the quarter.
=> END

~ offer_accept_executive_party_money
% {{name}}: Sensible. The treasurer will hear from my office tomorrow. I trust we understand each other well enough to spare ourselves further ceremony.
% {{name}}: I am glad practical people can settle practical matters. You will find my firm remembers its friends, and forgets to remember anything else.
% {{name}}: You have my gratitude, and the wire transfer will follow. It has been a pleasure doing this in person, away from the noise.
=> END

~ offer_refuse_executive_party_money
% {{name}}: Of course. Forget I raised the matter. I would hate a clumsy gesture to spoil what was, until now, a civil conversation.
% {{name}}: I misjudged the room, it seems. My firm will pursue its interests through the usual channels. Forgive the habits of an old trader.
% {{name}}: As you wish. I shall say I never mentioned money, and you may believe I never did. Good day, {{president}}.
=> END

~ offer_executive_personal_wealth
% {{name}}: Beyond my request, there is a personal matter. My board is establishing an advisory arrangement, and your name would honour it. The fees are, frankly, generous.
% {{name}}: People in your position are not in office forever. A small investment opportunity exists, and I would be pleased to reserve a place in it for you.
% {{name}}: Consider it a token between people who ought to be allies. My firm values counsel such as yours, and it pays for what it values.
=> END

~ offer_accept_executive_personal_wealth
% {{name}}: Then the papers will be drawn up quietly. No one need ever connect them to this conversation, and no one will.
% {{name}}: I confess I hoped you would see the sense of it. The arrangement will be discreet, regular, and entirely yours.
% {{name}}: Very good. You will find us punctual payers and silent partners. Which, in my trade, is the highest of compliments.
=> END

~ offer_refuse_executive_personal_wealth
% {{name}}: A principled president. How refreshing, and how inconvenient. My apologies for presuming upon your time.
% {{name}}: Then we shall speak only of my original request, and never again of arrangements. Some doors are best left unopened.
% {{name}}: I withdraw the suggestion entirely, and my admiration for your reputation survives intact. Barely.
=> END

~ offer_press_owner_personal_wealth
% {{name}}: My editors are thorough people, {{president}}. A paper's judgment benefits from friendship, and friendship benefits from, let us say, mutual investment.
% {{name}}: I own newspapers, and I own them for a living. A private arrangement between us would let my columnists write with, shall we say, better judgment about {{ask}}.
% {{name}}: Coverage follows climate, and climate is something two reasonable people can arrange. A gesture toward your personal foundation would go far in that direction.
=> END

~ offer_accept_press_owner_personal_wealth
% {{name}}: Then the weather over your affairs will be mild. My readers will barely recognize the change, which is rather the point.
% {{name}}: Wise. You will find the morning editions gentler than the season has led you to expect. Consider it a standing arrangement.
% {{name}}: I am pleased we could settle this like publishers and statesmen. The news cycle, I promise, will show its gratitude.
=> END

~ offer_refuse_press_owner_personal_wealth
% {{name}}: A pity. Then my journalists must simply follow their instincts, wherever those may lead them. We shall see what they find.
% {{name}}: I offered friendship, nothing more, and I shall not insult you by insisting. The presses run regardless, as you know.
% {{name}}: As you wish. I misjudged you, and one rarely misjudges twice. Do enjoy the Sunday edition.
=> END

~ affair_why_unmarried
% {{name}}: Secrecy? For what, exactly? You have no spouse to spare any blushes, {{president}}, and I have no patience for theatre. Dinner on Friday, in public, like honest people.
% {{name}}: You keep bracing for scandal, and there is none to be had. You are unattached and so am I. We may simply be ordinary about this.
% {{name}}: If you were married, this whispering might have some charm. As it stands, I see only someone fumbling to ask me to dinner. So ask properly.
=> END

~ affair_why_spouse
% {{name}}: An affair, with the person you married. That would be a novelty. Perhaps you should court me again, {{president}}, instead of negotiating with me.
% {{name}}: Whatever you are proposing, I already have it, ring and certificate included. Though I confess I miss being pursued. You may bring flowers.
% {{name}}: You want discretion from your own spouse. That is either very sad or very flattering, and tonight I choose flattering. Come home early.
=> END

~ affair_why_no_spark
% {{name}}: You are not unattractive, and I am not offended. But whatever this is supposed to feel like, I do not feel it, and I doubt you do either.
% {{name}}: Let us be kind and be done with it. I admire you, I enjoy your company, and nothing more will come of standing this close. That is simply how it is.
% {{name}}: There is no version of this that works. Not for lack of courage, only for lack of warmth on both sides. I would rather keep your friendship than pretend.
=> END

~ affair_why_too_cold
% {{name}}: I think we both know better. There has been nothing between us but formal words for ages, and formal words do not lead where you imagine.
% {{name}}: Whatever this was once, it has since cooled past reviving. I will thank you not to embarrass us both by trying.
% {{name}}: You mistake courtesy for interest, {{president}}. They are distant cousins at best. Let us keep this audience official.
=> END

~ affair_begin
% {{name}}: Very well. But we will be careful, and we will be dull about it. No notes, no telephones, and never the same place twice.
% {{name}}: Then it is understood between us, and understood nowhere else. I find I do not need persuading, only assurances.
% {{name}}: I accept, on condition that we are neither of us sentimental about it. Whatever happens in this room stays outside history.
=> END

~ affair_end
% {{name}}: I will not make a scene, and I will not ask twice. But you might have spared me the speech. That part was unnecessary.
% {{name}}: So it ends the way it began, with you deciding and me agreeing. I would say I regret it, and on most days I nearly would.
% {{name}}: I understand, and understanding is the worst part. You will find me correct at every function. Correct is all I intend to be.
=> END

~ lie_caught
% {{name}}: The figures I was shown this morning say otherwise. I will assume you were misinformed, and leave it there, for now.
% {{name}}: You have never lied to me before, and I did not enjoy the novelty. Shall we try the question again, or is my time being spent for nothing?
% {{name}}: I came here with trust and a folder. The folder proved better company. Tell me, was any of today true?
=> END

~ lie_uncaught
% {{name}}: If you say so. You would know better than I, I am sure.
% {{name}}: Of course. Your version has the advantage of coming from you, and that is enough for me. We will leave it there.
% {{name}}: I believe you, {{president}}, or at least I will act exactly as if I did. In politics that amounts to the same courtesy.
=> END

~ lever_bargain_backroom_success
% {{name}}: Now that is a language I understand. A quiet word from you, and suddenly committees discover their conscience. Nothing on paper, naturally.
% {{name}}: Elegant. The right person finds themselves on the right board, the right file moves to the right desk, and no one can point to a thing. I accept.
% {{name}}: No money changes hands and nothing is asked in the open. That is how real business is done. You have my full agreement.
=> END

~ lever_bargain_backroom_failure
% {{name}}: A favour in the shadows is still a debt, and debts in the dark cost double. I would rather have less, in daylight, than that.
% {{name}}: You are offering me an arrangement I could not survive being seen holding. So no, {{president}}. It is too clever for me.
% {{name}}: If it went wrong, it would go wrong for both of us, and I would fall further. Find another currency or find another buyer.
=> END

~ lever_bargain_aid_success
% {{name}}: So the line stays in the budget, but bends in our direction. I have always admired how flexible public money becomes in determined hands.
% {{name}}: A programme for one purpose, quietly serving another. The auditors will see devotion, and I will see results. We are agreed.
% {{name}}: That will do nicely. Nothing announced, nothing signed, merely a sum that wanders off its intended path. Consider my support secured.
=> END

~ lever_bargain_aid_failure
% {{name}}: Diverted money leaves a trail, and trails end in hearings. I will not build my cause on your bookkeeping.
% {{name}}: You are asking me to be grateful for funds that could hang us both. Too thin, {{president}}, and far too risky.
% {{name}}: I have watched better people than you fall over redirected budget lines. Offer me nothing rather than that.
=> END
